            <ArticleTitle>[Minimally invasive injection therapy in lumbar syndromes].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-58</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Minimally invasive injection therapy is an effective approach for the treatment of sciatica with less complications. This therapy is a sufficient option in cases without absolute indications for operation.The paper describes in detail the different injection techniques like spinal nerve analgesia, epidural dorsal/perineural injections, vertebral joint infiltrations, and radiculographies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
